<title>USA: Oregon $4.5 mln housing deal ylds 6.20 pct in 2028.</title>
<headline>Oregon $4.5 mln housing deal ylds 6.20 pct in 2028.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc said Tuesday it tentatively priced $4.5 million Oregon Housing and Community Services Department housing bonds at a top yield of 6.20 percent in 2028.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>STATE OF OREGON</p>
<p>RE: $4,500,000*</p>
<p>HOUSING AND COMMUNITY SERVICES DEPARTMENT</p>
<p>MULTIFAMILY HOUSING REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>1996 SERIES A</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE CHANGE IN SCALE IN MATURITIES 2011 THROUGH 2028.</p>
<p>SUBJECT TO ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX</p>
<p>	MOODY'S: Aa		    S&amp;P: NR</p>
<p>	DATED: 09/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 07/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
